1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,080
Listen to a talk on a history podcast.

2
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:11,180
In the 19th century, cities in the United States became crowded.

3
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:16,150
Many businesses and apartments were housed in tall buildings.

4
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:19,080
Fires became a major concern.

5
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:22,560
Most firetruck ladders only reached the fourth floor,

6
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:24,210
which wasn't high enough.

7
00:00:24,210 --> 00:00:32,036
Although laws were passed to require escape routes, many early ideas were impractical, like

8
00:00:32,036 --> 00:00:36,070
one idea was to attach a parachute to your head.

9
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:41,140
The parachute idea, well, this wouldn't work too well, would it?

10
00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:44,260
Other such ideas were met with resistance, too.

11
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:47,593
Enter Anna Connolly,

12
00:00:47,593 --> 00:00:52,110
who received patents for fire escapes in the 19th century.

13
00:00:52,110 --> 00:00:58,750
Anna Connolly's initial fire escape design was a bridge so people could safely go up to the roof

14
00:00:58,750 --> 00:01:02,763
or upper floors of their own building, cross to the building next door,

15
00:01:02,763 --> 00:01:05,110
and go down the stairs there.

16
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:10,150
This made good sense since most fires started on the lower floors of buildings.

17
00:01:10,150 --> 00:01:17,151
After this design, Connolly created another that was a series of platforms attached to

18
00:01:17,151 --> 00:01:20,160
the side of a building with ladders connecting them.

19
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:27,100
She specified they'd be made of iron, since iron is fireproof and resists pressure.

20
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:30,265
Well, this design worked, was practical,

21
00:01:30,265 --> 00:01:32,220
and was adopted across the country.

22
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:36,210
Connolly's fire escapes saved lives.

23
00:01:36,210 --> 00:01:44,212
These days, buildings in the US are built with interior stairwells that are fireproof for escape

24
00:01:44,212 --> 00:01:47,000
and are not visible from the outside.

25
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:54,020
But you can still see Connolly's design on older buildings in cities.
